# Shell scripts and git hooks must check out with LF, always.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where core.autocrlf rewrites text files to
# CRLF on checkout. A shell script that lands with CRLF has "#!/bin/sh\r" as its
# shebang, and Linux and macOS answer that with "bad interpreter: No such file
# or directory". The scripts below are the ones an adopter installs and CI runs,
# so they are the ones that must not carry a carriage return.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
